Chinese 位 means a position, rank, bit, or a polite counter for people.
Its person-count compounds are strong; longer place/unit compounds are weaker.
English position/location, coordinates, seats, bits, digits and 'another'
share smaller signals. A few translations and position abbreviations also
respond. Split words are joined, and 'position of' retains a smaller response.
This predicts lexical responses, not actual spatial coordinates.
