"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3096: a "ni" syllable detector.

It reads the current token alone and fires when that token sounds like the syllable "ni":
  - a single katakana / hanja / hangul "ni" character (ニ 尼 니 妮): strongest;
  - the bare syllable (ni, ní, ни, ня, Ni, NI, ني) and short Latin fragments ending
    in -ni / -nie / -nil, with an optional vowel before (ani, ini, oni, uni, nil, nie): strong;
  - short Cyrillic fragments built on ни/ня (ани, ени, нич, ник): medium;
  - the hiragana particle に: weak;
  - longer Latin fragments built on ni (anic, ania, nite, unit, nice): weak.
Everything else gets 0, including longer English words that contain "ni" (united,
university) and Cyrillic words such as -ение. It ignores context.
"""
