"""Approximate an at-sign detector with weaker annotation punctuation responses.

Bare @ tokens in emails, handles and decorators are strongest. The
response changes when the same token includes brackets, quotes, a word,
or doubled signs. Fullwidth ＠ also responds. Hashes inside lines,
macro definitions, documentation comments and copyright marks have
weaker positive responses. Other text is predicted as zero: this leaves
the component's small, scattered lexical responses unexplained.
