What it does, in plain terms: it switches on at three kinds of token.
  1. The end-of-document token <|endoftext|>: strong (about 1.05).
  2. The word "what" / "What" (the question or relative word): strong (about 1.1).
  3. A full stop that closes an abbreviation or an initial, such as "Mr.", "U.S.",
