Fires on a dash, opening parenthesis, semicolon, colon, spaced hyphen or opening
square bracket that comes right after a word and interrupts a sentence that is already
under way: "... the trading strategy — ...", "... the rules (which ...". It is strongest
for dashes and parentheses, weaker for colons, and near zero for the same marks in code,
maths or number ranges (where the surrounding tokens are not plain words), and near zero
at the start of a sentence. Predicts 0 everywhere else.
