"""Approximate the component's strongest responses with readable text rules.

Isolated macron vowels, especially ā, dominate. Circumflex and caron
vowels, three Latvian consonants, and a Hindi long-aa token fragment
have smaller positive responses. Capitalization before ā and leading
spaces modify the vowel responses. Completed byte-split macron letters
are recognized from the decoded prefix. The fragment 'ums' is positive;
'with' after forms of 'come', or 'come up', is negative. State resets
between documents. Other, diffuse responses are omitted: predict zero.
