"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3131 — a "number-start 0" detector.

Fires on the digit 0 when it begins a standalone number (after a space, bracket, comma or
operator): about +1.2. A 0 that continues a number (after another digit) stays at 0; a 0 in
a decimal fraction (1.0) is weak (+0.3); a 0 in a version string (v0.1) or after \\x / \\u
is 0. Inside \\x byte escapes (\\xe2\\x80\\x99) the digits 8, 9, 0 right after \\x go
negative (-2), and the 2 of a lead byte \\xc2 / \\xe2 goes to -1.2. The word-piece "am" that
completes "Hu-am-n" (Human) is +2.5. Everything else is 0."""
